    {
      "id": "n1",
      "kind": "grammar",
      "title": "जाते हैं, बेचती हैं",
      "text": "These are the \"do it regularly\" forms: a verb stem + -ता, -ती or -ते, then है / हैं / हूँ. The ending follows who does it: हम जाते हैं; a man says मैं जाता हूँ and a woman मैं जाती हूँ; Seeta Nani (a woman, respected) बेचती हैं. The same form is used for something happening now or soon.",
      "explains": [
        "hi.present-habitual"
      ],
      "afterScenes": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "n2",
      "kind": "usage",
      "title": "चलो",
      "text": "चलो is \"come on, let's go\". It is an easy, friendly request to people you call तुम; to someone you call आप you would say चलिए.",
      "explains": [
        "hi.imperative-chalo"
      ],
      "afterScenes": 0
    }
  ],
